\viewkind4\uc1\pard\cf1\ul\b\f0\fs24\'b6 Verse 1\cf0\ulnone\b0 
\par 1. Look from Thy sphere of endless day,
\par O God of mercy and of might;
\par In pity look on those who stray
\par Benighted in this land of light.
\par 
\par \cf1\ul\b\'b6 Verse 2\cf0\ulnone\b0 
\par 2. In peopled vale, in lonely glen,
\par In crowded mart, by stream or sea,
\par How many of the sons of men
\par Hear not the message sent from Thee.
\par 
\par \cf1\ul\b\'b6 Verse 3\cf0\ulnone\b0 
\par 3. Send forth Thy heralds, Lord, to call
\par The thoughtless young, the hardened old,
\par A scattered homeless flock, till all
\par Be gathered to Thy peaceful fold.
\par 
\par \cf1\ul\b\'b6 Verse 4\cf0\ulnone\b0 
\par 4. Send them Thy mighty word to speak,
\par Till faith shall dawn and doubt depart,
\par To awe the bold, to stay the weak,
\par And bind and heal the broken heart.
\par 
\par \cf1\ul\b\'b6 Verse 5\cf0\ulnone\b0  
\par 5. Then all these wastes, a dreary scene,
\par That make us sadden as we gaze,
\par Shall grow, with living waters, green,
\par And lift to heaven the voice of praise.\f1 
\par \cf1\ul\b\fs16 
\par }

